trait-tomte-headgear = Tomte headgear weight
trait-tomte-headgear-rule = A helmet or crown heavier than 1.0 lb reduces Intelligence and device skill, and disables Tomte automatic sensing and level-40 identification. Automatic identification from other sources is unaffected. Other headgear can still be worn.
trait-race-effects = Racial traits
trait-ent-rule-basics = Base attributes: STR +2, WIS +2, DEX −3, CON +2; life 105%, base HP 25, experience requirement 135%; one level of poison resistance.
trait-ent-rule-growth = At levels 26, 41 and 46, gain +1 STR and CON and lose 1 DEX each time. These bonuses follow current level and form.
trait-ent-rule-digging = Without a melee weapon equipped, gain level ×10 digging skill. Digging tools also disable this bonus; shields and launchers do not.
trait-ent-rule-fire = Nonnegative fire reduction below immunity is multiplied by 70% and rounded down (50% →35%). Inventory is also more vulnerable to fire. Zero, negative resistance and immunity remain unchanged.
trait-ent-rule-diet = Ordinary food provides 1/20 nutrition. Native Ents with no temporary form gain 4200 nutrition from water, capped at 14999. Other potions also apply special nutrition after their main effect. Temporary Ent forms receive only the potion's original nutrition.
trait-ent-rule-forest = Move directly through trees at normal action cost. Mounted movement still respects the mount's terrain restrictions.
trait-ent-rule-power = At level 10, gain Summon Tree: WIS, base cost 20, base failure 70%. Before level 45, randomly attempt one tree. From level 45, base cost is 50 and all surrounding squares are attempted. This creates terrain; an empty result still spends resources.
trait-ent-rule-birth = Start with 15–23 potions of water, 3–7 torches and class equipment, without ordinary rations. The racial virtue is Nature.
trait-tonberry-rule-basics = Basic traits: sustains Strength and Constitution, resists fear, and has 2 tiles of infravision.
trait-tonberry-rule-speed = Speed: starts at −1; drops by 1 at levels 30, 40, 45 and 50.
trait-tonberry-rule-damage = Weapon damage: the active melee weapon gains twice your level per hit.
trait-tonberry-rule-attacks = Weapon attacks: lose 0.04 attacks per level per melee action, down to zero. Neither weapon adjustment affects unarmed, innate or ranged attacks.
trait-tonberry-rule-confusion = Confusion resistance: positive resistance below immunity becomes (percent + 1) / 2, rounded down. Zero resistance, vulnerability and immunity are unchanged.
trait-tonberry-rule-birth = Birth traits: native Tonberries can master the sabre and start with Individualism.
trait-tomte-headgear-heavy = Headgear too heavy: Intelligence and device skill penalized; racial sensing and identification disabled
trait-tomte-headgear-light = Headgear within limit: automatic sensing active; automatic identification from level 40
trait-free-action = Free action
trait-free-action-rule = The core represents this protection as paralysis immunity and also consults it for some slowing effects. It does not stack by source count or prevent every action restriction; hunger fainting can still occur.
trait-sustain-rule = Protects against applicable drains of this attribute; it does not raise the value or stack by source count. Special costs follow their own rules.
trait-sense-rule = Indicates the sensing capability, not guaranteed visibility. Target category, mental traits, distance and current map rules still restrict detection. Source counts do not stack.
trait-targeted-sense-rule = Checks the target category and distance without telepathy's mental-trait filter. It does not detect unrelated categories or infinitely distant targets, and source counts do not stack.
trait-see-invisible-rule = Source count participates in see-invisible checks; detection is not guaranteed and does not bypass every visibility restriction.
trait-hold-life-rule = Source count is used for experience-drain protection, not HP recovery or damage immunity.
